ication (The OFR index marks this order 'not received for publication', so it was probably never printed in the Federal Register (OFR catalog statement, not verified here). Other routes: NARA, presidential lib); 1 compiled-transcription lead(s) (for example Richardson) point to the text but are not the original by themselves"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Whereas, in my judgment, the public interest requires that Nelson S. Thompson, Chief, Mechanical Engineering Section, Office of the Supervising Architect, Public Buildings Administration, Federal Works Agency, who, during the month of September, 1940, will reach the retirement age prescribed for automatic separation from the service, applicable to him, be exempted from compulsory retirement for age for a period of one year:\n\nNow, Therefore, by virtue of and pursuant to the authority vested in me by section 204 of the act of June 30, 1932, 47 Stat. 382, 404 (U.S.C., title 5, sec. 715a), I hereby exempt the said Nelson S. Thompson from compulsory retirement for age for a period of one year ending September 30, 1941.\n\nFRANKLIN D ROOSEVELT\n\nThe White House,\n\nMay 7, 1940.\n","path":"jobs/app-executive-orders/output/texts/executive-order-8402-exemption-nelson-s-thompson-from-compulsory-retirement-for-age.txt","sha256":"57ad7b15c01e5156491e33823137e74178f2f43dfbce49ac76947234f0094c0a","source":{"line":8290,"path":"jobs/app-transcriptions/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"7bc3f8add5cad4655f95a2a9af1bd05d072d1d79faf824b3475aee2b1fffadaf"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Executive Order 8402—Exemption of Nelson S. Thompson From Compulsory Retirement for Age\n\nWhereas, in my judgment, the public interest requires that Nelson S. Thompson, Chief, Mechanical Engineering Section, Office of the Supervising Architect, Public Buildings Administration, Federal Works Agency, who, during the month of September, 1940, will reach the retirement age prescribed for automatic separation from the service, applicable to him, be exempted from compulsory retirement for age for a period of one year:\n\nNow, Therefore, by virtue of and pursuant to the authority vested in me by section 204 of the act of June 30, 1932, 47 Stat. 382, 404 (U.S.C., title 5, sec. 715a), I hereby exempt the said Nelson S. Thompson from compulsory retirement for age for a period of one year ending September 30, 1941.\n\nFRANKLIN D ROOSEVELT\n\nThe White House,\n\nMay 7, 1940.","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-app-executive-orders-8402-23c8a9bd8a.txt","sha256":"13d084a84e53121390351d40776f34f21a5402fc8ce814e6544b67040cf53924","source":{"line":3817,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"0c7ca30c2acb5d19b87e5e00e67b2afb23af51ea9c0b5ede2ac2a100d8bb0844"}}]}
